;; errors.corpus -- C3g (typed, multi-clause `catch`): promoted out of
;; tests/conformance/pending/errors.corpus once mova's engine gained
;; genuine class-dispatched `catch` (`eval::special_forms::
;; catch_class_matches`). Before C3g, `try` supported exactly one
;; UNTYPED catch clause, so this form -- three clauses, the first two
;; deliberately non-matching -- always hit mova's "try: only one catch
;; clause is supported" error and diverged from real Clojure, which picks
;; the first matching clause (`ArithmeticException`, the actual class a
;; division by zero throws) and evaluates to `:ae`. Both sides now agree.
(try (/ 1 0) (catch ClassCastException e :cce) (catch ArithmeticException e :ae) (catch Exception e :generic))

;; W-ERR (field2, host application field report): promoted out of
;; tests/conformance/pending/errors.corpus once `core.mova` gained a real
;; `ex-cause` (mirroring `ex-message`'s established `ex-info`/host-
;; `Throwable` polymorphic pattern). Before W-ERR, `ex-cause` did not
;; exist at all ("Unable to resolve symbol: ex-cause"). Both sides now
;; agree: the outer `ex-info`'s cause is the inner `ex-info`, and its
;; message is `"inner"`.
(ex-message (ex-cause (ex-info "outer" {} (ex-info "inner" {}))))
